Here's the same service rewritten to build the query JSON yourself, call Elasticsearch over plain HTTP, and map the response into your own objects. I'm using Spring's `RestClient` (Spring 6.1 / Boot 3.2+) — **not** Elastic's `org.elasticsearch.client.RestClient`, watch the import. A `RestTemplate` variant is noted at the end.

## 1. HTTP client config

```java
@Configuration
public class ElasticConfig {

    @Bean
    public RestClient elasticRestClient(@Value("${elastic.url}") String url,           // e.g. https://es-host:9200
                                        @Value("${elastic.username}") String user,
                                        @Value("${elastic.password}") String pass) {
        return RestClient.builder()
                .baseUrl(url)
                .defaultHeaders(h -> {
                    h.setBasicAuth(user, pass);
                    h.setContentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON);
                    h.setAccept(List.of(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON));
                })
                .defaultStatusHandler(HttpStatusCode::isError, (req, res) -> {
                    String body = new String(res.getBody().readAllBytes(), StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
                    throw new ElasticException(res.getStatusCode().value(), body);
                })
                .build();
    }
}

public class ElasticException extends RuntimeException {
    public ElasticException(int status, String body) { super("ES " + status + ": " + body); }
}
```

## 2. Response models (what ES returns)

```java
@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)
public record EsSearchResponse(
        @JsonProperty("pit_id") String pitId,
        EsHits hits,
        JsonNode aggregations) {}          // aggs are heterogenous -> keep as tree, map below

@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)
public record EsHits(EsTotal total, List<EsHit> hits) {}

@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)
public record EsTotal(long value, String relation) {}

@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)
public record EsHit(
        @JsonProperty("_id") String id,
        @JsonProperty("_source") ExpressionDoc source,
        List<JsonNode> sort) {}            // search_after cursor, echoed back as-is

public record EsPitResponse(String id) {}
```

Your domain DTOs (`ExpressionDoc`, `NumberType`, `DataSourceStats`, `PhoneSummary`) stay as in the previous answer. `ExpressionPage` changes only in the cursor type:

```java
public record ExpressionPage(
        List<ExpressionDoc> items,
        String pitId,
        List<JsonNode> searchAfter,        // e.g. [1726000000000, 4711]
        boolean hasMore) {}

public record ExpressionPageRequest(
        String number,
        NumberType type,                   // nullable
        Integer size,
        String pitId,                      // nullable on first call
        List<JsonNode> searchAfter) {}     // nullable on first call
```

## 3. Query factory (builds the request JSON)

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class EsQueryFactory {

    private static final String KEEP_ALIVE = "2m";
    private final ObjectMapper om;

    // ---- discriminating query: phone vs mobile vs unknown ----
    public ObjectNode numberQuery(String number, @Nullable NumberType type) {
        ObjectNode q = om.createObjectNode();
        if (type != null) {
            q.putObject("term").put(type == NumberType.MOBILE ? "mobile" : "phone", number);
            return q;
        }
        ObjectNode bool = q.putObject("bool");
        ArrayNode should = bool.putArray("should");
        should.addObject().putObject("term").put("phone", number);
        should.addObject().putObject("term").put("mobile", number);
        bool.put("minimum_should_match", 1);
        return q;
    }

    // ---- summary: count + last + byType + byDataSource ----
    public ObjectNode summaryQuery(String number, @Nullable NumberType type) {
        ObjectNode root = om.createObjectNode();
        root.put("size", 0);
        root.put("track_total_hits", true);
        root.set("query", numberQuery(number, type));

        ObjectNode aggs = root.putObject("aggs");
        aggs.set("last", lastTopHit());

        ObjectNode byType = aggs.putObject("byType").putObject("filters").putObject("filters");
        byType.putObject("PHONE").putObject("exists").put("field", "phone");
        byType.putObject("MOBILE").putObject("exists").put("field", "mobile");

        ObjectNode byDs = aggs.putObject("byDataSource");
        byDs.putObject("terms").put("field", "dataSource").put("size", 200);
        byDs.putObject("aggs").set("last", lastTopHit());
        return root;
    }

    private ObjectNode lastTopHit() {
        ObjectNode agg = om.createObjectNode();
        ObjectNode th = agg.putObject("top_hits");
        th.put("size", 1);
        th.putArray("sort").addObject().putObject("insertionDate").put("order", "desc");
        return agg;
    }

    // ---- one page via PIT + search_after ----
    public ObjectNode pageQuery(String number, @Nullable NumberType type, int size,
                                String pitId, @Nullable List<JsonNode> searchAfter) {
        ObjectNode root = om.createObjectNode();
        root.put("size", size);
        root.put("track_total_hits", false);
        root.set("query", numberQuery(number, type));
        root.putArray("sort").addObject().putObject("insertionDate").put("order", "desc");
        root.putObject("pit").put("id", pitId).put("keep_alive", KEEP_ALIVE);
        root.putArray("_source").add("phone").add("mobile").add("expression")
                                .add("dataSource").add("insertionDate");
        if (searchAfter != null && !searchAfter.isEmpty()) {
            root.putArray("search_after").addAll(searchAfter);
        }
        return root;
    }

    public ObjectNode closePitBody(String pitId) {
        return om.createObjectNode().put("id", pitId);
    }
}
```

