## 4. Service (REST calls + mapping to objects)

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PhoneExpressionService {

    private static final String INDEX = "phone-expressions";
    private static final String KEEP_ALIVE = "2m";

    private final RestClient es;            // org.springframework.web.client.RestClient
    private final EsQueryFactory queries;
    private final ObjectMapper om;

    // ---------------- Summary ----------------
    public PhoneSummary getSummary(String number, @Nullable NumberType type) {

        EsSearchResponse resp = es.post()
                .uri("/{index}/_search?routing={r}", INDEX, number)   // drop routing param if not used
                .body(queries.summaryQuery(number, type))
                .retrieve()
                .body(EsSearchResponse.class);

        long total = resp.hits() != null && resp.hits().total() != null
                ? resp.hits().total().value() : 0L;

        JsonNode aggs = resp.aggregations();
        ExpressionDoc last = firstTopHit(aggs.path("last"));

        JsonNode typeBuckets = aggs.path("byType").path("buckets");
        long mobileCount = typeBuckets.path("MOBILE").path("doc_count").asLong();
        long phoneCount  = typeBuckets.path("PHONE").path("doc_count").asLong();
        NumberType resolved = mobileCount > 0 ? NumberType.MOBILE
                            : phoneCount  > 0 ? NumberType.PHONE
                            : type;

        List<DataSourceStats> perSource = new ArrayList<>();
        for (JsonNode b : aggs.path("byDataSource").path("buckets")) {
            perSource.add(new DataSourceStats(
                    b.path("key").asText(),
                    b.path("doc_count").asLong(),
                    firstTopHit(b.path("last"))));
        }

        return new PhoneSummary(number, resolved, total, last, perSource);
    }

    private ExpressionDoc firstTopHit(JsonNode topHitsAgg) {
        JsonNode hits = topHitsAgg.path("hits").path("hits");
        if (!hits.isArray() || hits.isEmpty()) return null;
        return om.convertValue(hits.get(0).path("_source"), ExpressionDoc.class);
    }

    // ---------------- Paged expressions ----------------
    public ExpressionPage getExpressions(ExpressionPageRequest req) {

        int size = req.size() == null ? 100 : Math.min(req.size(), 1000);
        String pit = req.pitId() != null ? req.pitId() : openPit(req.number());

        EsSearchResponse resp = es.post()
                .uri("/_search")                                       // no index in path when using PIT
                .body(queries.pageQuery(req.number(), req.type(), size, pit, req.searchAfter()))
                .retrieve()
                .body(EsSearchResponse.class);

        List<EsHit> hits = resp.hits() == null ? List.of() : resp.hits().hits();
        List<ExpressionDoc> items = hits.stream().map(EsHit::source).toList();

        boolean hasMore = hits.size() == size;
        List<JsonNode> next = hasMore ? hits.get(hits.size() - 1).sort() : null;

        if (!hasMore) closePit(resp.pitId());

        return new ExpressionPage(items, hasMore ? resp.pitId() : null, next, hasMore);
    }

    private String openPit(String number) {
        EsPitResponse r = es.post()
                .uri("/{index}/_pit?keep_alive={ka}&routing={r}", INDEX, KEEP_ALIVE, number)
                .retrieve()
                .body(EsPitResponse.class);
        return r.id();
    }

    public void closePit(@Nullable String pitId) {
        if (pitId == null) return;
        try {
            es.method(HttpMethod.DELETE)          // delete() has no body(), so use method()
              .uri("/_pit")
              .body(queries.closePitBody(pitId))
              .retrieve()
              .toBodilessEntity();
        } catch (RuntimeException ignored) { /* best effort; PIT expires anyway */ }
    }

    // ---------------- Full server-side iteration (export etc.) ----------------
    public void forEachExpression(String number, @Nullable NumberType type, Consumer<ExpressionDoc> consumer) {
        ExpressionPage page = getExpressions(new ExpressionPageRequest(number, type, 1000, null, null));
        while (true) {
            page.items().forEach(consumer);
            if (!page.hasMore()) break;
            page = getExpressions(new ExpressionPageRequest(number, type, 1000, page.pitId(), page.searchAfter()));
        }
    }
}
```

## 5. Controller

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/numbers")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PhoneExpressionController {

    private final PhoneExpressionService service;

    @GetMapping("/{number}/summary")
    public PhoneSummary summary(@PathVariable String number,
                                @RequestParam(required = false) NumberType type) {
        return service.getSummary(number, type);
    }

    // POST because the search_after cursor is a JSON array (mixed number types)
    @PostMapping("/expressions")
    public ExpressionPage expressions(@RequestBody ExpressionPageRequest req) {
        return service.getExpressions(req);
    }

    @DeleteMapping("/expressions/pit")
    public void closePit(@RequestParam String pitId) {
        service.closePit(pitId);
    }
}
```

UI flow: `GET /summary` once → `POST /expressions` with `{number, type, size}` → keep posting back the returned `pitId` + `searchAfter` untouched until `hasMore == false`.

## Notes

- **Endpoints used:** `POST /{index}/_search`, `POST /{index}/_pit?keep_alive=2m`, `POST /_search` (with `pit` in body), `DELETE /_pit` (with `{"id": ...}` body). All plain JSON, no client library.
- **`insertionDate` → `Instant`:** Spring Boot registers `JavaTimeModule` automatically, so ISO-8601 strings or epoch millis in `_source` both deserialize. If your dates are stored in a custom format, add `@JsonFormat(pattern = "...")` on the field.
- **Why `JsonNode` for aggregations:** aggregation responses vary by type; mapping them by path is simpler and less brittle than modelling every shape. Hits are fully typed.
- **Why keep `sort` as `List<JsonNode>`:** the cursor contains a date (epoch millis) and `_shard_doc` (long). Passing it back verbatim avoids any type/format conversion issues.
- **RestTemplate instead of RestClient** (older Spring): replace each call with
  `restTemplate.postForObject(url, new HttpEntity<>(body, headers), EsSearchResponse.class)` and for close-PIT use `restTemplate.exchange(url, HttpMethod.DELETE, new HttpEntity<>(body, headers), Void.class)`.
- **Security:** if your cluster uses API keys instead of basic auth, swap `setBasicAuth` for `h.set("Authorization", "ApiKey " + encodedKey)`.
